From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:46:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL_TIER_ROWS, the g53
 schedule knobs on big prompt windows only

Under TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL=g53 (glm53f-afd's large-M expert prompt kernels, written by Hugh Madden, glm53f-afd @
91db3cc), the configuration knobs (TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL_MT, _GW, _NT, _L2, _FUSE, _DISCARD) set one schedule for
every prompt window. On GB10, glm53f-rank's own above-2,048-row schedule (mt 4, gw 16, nt 4, l2 1) runs about 5 %
faster than the default on 2,048-row windows but 4-10 % slower on 256-1,024-row ones, so set for every window it
costs the smaller windows part of what it gains on the full ones.

- TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL_TIER_ROWS=N (1..4,096): the knobs' schedule runs windows of at least N rows only, and smaller
  windows keep default_cfg's. Unset or empty: the knobs apply to every window, as before.
- Bits: the fields it tiers keep every bit, and a row's bits do not depend on its window, so a row gets the same bits
  on either side of N. It tiers only those same-bits fields: with _SK, _SKD or _SWIGLU set it refuses at the node's
  start.
- The node's start line names it ("; schedule <fields> for windows of N-<widest> rows, default_cfg's for 1-<N - 1>
  (tier TF_GLM_EXPERT_KERNEL_TIER_ROWS=N; the same bits)"); with no knob set it says every window runs default_cfg.

Tests: tests/test_glm_g53_tier.py (CPU: the name; unset as before; the split at N for every window size 1-4,096 with
one set of bit fields; refusals, read only under g53; the node's calls and start line; and tests/glm_g53_schedule.py's
emulated decomposition at 1,024- and 2,048-row windows with N 1,536 and mt 4 gw 16 nt 4 l2 1: a row's bits are the
same in either window and equal to the default schedule's). tests/cuda/test_glm_g53_kernel.py gains the GPU byte
check of windows of 1,024-2,048 rows on either side of N for N 1,280-2,048, and TF_G53_TUNE_ROWS / TF_G53_TUNE_N for
its times report. The g53 test files clear the new variable too.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (planning and execution), via Hermes

